    "physical_description": "Woman's longyi made of silk with a floating weft weave. It consists of a tube made up of a warp length of cloth sewn by hand across a weft seam, so that the warp runs horizontally around the body of the wearer. Dark red ground with weft yellow acheik (horizontal wave) patterns in 'joe gee jay' style ('jay' means hook or line). The pattern of these bands is of several parallel wavy lines, broken by a diagonal bar with a single blossom within the waves;  of three wavy bands; and broken interwoven lines, in a sequence.",
